'A translator was asked to prepare an English description of a local festival for two audiences. The first version would appear on a sign for visitors who knew little about the event. The second would accompany a detailed article for readers interested in its history. Some cultural terms had no single English equivalent that conveyed every association. Rather than force the same wording into both versions, the translator kept a local term where it mattered and explained it in language suited to each audience. The short sign focused on what visitors could observe, while the article included more historical context. Neither version could reproduce every meaning carried by the original text. The translator therefore recorded a few choices and checked them with the organisers, making the purpose of each version explicit.',
[('Why did the translator use different wording?',['The audiences and purposes differed','English has no cultural words','The organisers banned explanations','The original festival had changed dates'],0,4),('What did the translator check with organisers?',['A few translation choices','The readers\' passport numbers','The price of printing only','The length of the queue'],0,7)],
